{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And I shall give it to you.</b> In these three words Scripture explains that the proper Name YHWH promises to give the designated Land to Israel, who are a designated people — this is what is meant by ואני אתננה לכם. For that Land is Mine and you are My people in distinctiveness: I have not set over you any star or constellation, nor any angel or seraph, for you are My portion, not theirs; and I am Elohim to you, not to idolatry (עו\"ג); rather, I alone am to them the Elohim of Elohim. Thus explained the Ramban, of blessed memory; and although this is not his language, this is his intent."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:27:24.114208132Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}